{
  "id": "ss.char.dot",
  "name": "Dot",
  "description": "A survivor — a small person of the hive's brood, two heads tall, with a round frost-blue bob and the friendliest face of the eight. Big eyes with a glint, blush, a smile: the hive has none of that, because it never needed to look at anything, and a survivor whose scent organ has gone dead has nothing left but looking. The organ is still there, `dead`, worn as a brooch on the chest, and the two feelers still stand out of the hair — slate-grey, bobble-tipped, sweeping for a signal that never comes. Dot is the plain one: the round head it used to be is now the round head it has, and the lash — a Soldier's mandible on a cord — hangs coiled at the hip. Drawn facing +x; the game flips it.",
